[Round 3/8 | Implementer | 543.0s | 0/400k] I’m preserving global priority semantics by indexing every successful publication into the consumer heap, not only one item per producer. The per-lane publication stream is FIFO, while the heap contains its discovered live records; token state and owner validation still decide whether any record is real. A pre-claim advisory token hint closes the paused-after-claim gap, and a bounded lane repair can recover stale hints without entering the ordinary dequeue path.

